    "text": "actionnewsnow.com\nwebsite\nChico\nStorm Tracker Forecast: Air quality remains not the greatest as temperatures stay cooler\nBy Howie Gordon,\n1 hours agoSunny, hot and breezy (S 5 MPH but calm early) High pressure will begin moving closer and strengthening as we move into the weekend (Friday) allowing for ample sunshine and once again for temperatures to be on the rise. Light winds could become a little bit stronger after the weekend. After the weekend, temperatures look too cool again. Daytime Delta Breezes will keep moisture levels up while the switch to night time land (dry) breezes will keep the area on the drier side.",
